<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Truce of Plussa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1583</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Truce of Plussa was signed in August 1583 on the Plyussa River between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, ending the fighting between them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>. Sweden kept its conquests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a>, and the Ingrian fortresses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivangorod">Ivangorod</a>, Yam and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koporye">Koporye</a>. The truce was extended, but war resumed in 1590, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-teusina">Treaty of Teusina</a> of 1595 returned the Ingrian towns to Russia.</p></div>
